      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"McBehrer\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/mcbehrer/48/1850_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> McBehrer:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>WTAP + Looking Up is nice too. Especially with High Risk Behavior. Start of his turn, he loses 3 tokens to deal someone 3 damage, plus buffs.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>I’m not sure that works with high risk behavior. Wouldn’t the buffs be calculated before it figures out how many tokens to remove, meaning that you never have enough tokens to redirect it?</p>",
